# halyard — what never enters the repository.
#
# Since the 2026-09-12 tidy-up, the biggest section of this file is gone: the
# RE MATERIAL NO LONGER LIVES HERE AT ALL. Captures, Ghidra and IDA dumps, the
# official ShadowPCDisplay binary and the vendored FFmpeg tree moved beside the
# checkout, into a private lab directory beside it.
# That took the repo from 12 418 tracked files to 974.
#
# The rule that decides: RAW MATERIAL goes to the lab, CONCLUSIONS stay here.
# KB.md, memory/ and the 67 reports under tools/ida/out/ are the conclusions.

# --- the lab, should it ever be created inside the checkout by mistake ---
/shadow2switch-lab/

# --- capture output, wherever a tool drops it ---
# The first version of this rule listed only `captures_[0-9]*` and
# `captures_input_*`. The prefixes added later (scripted, manual, states) went
# straight through it, and 47 LFS files ended up tracked -- the policy was
# cancelled by its own pattern. Hence the wildcards.
/captures/
/captures_*/
**/*.pcap
**/sslkeys.log
PCAPdroid_*.pcap

# --- build artifacts (regenerable) ---
# WIN2 2026-10-02 - WILDCARDED, and for the second time in this file for the
# same reason. The list named the four blessed directories (linux, switch,
# windows, psv); `build_ft/` - the Windows build WITH file transfer - went
# straight through it, and brought 67 untracked files with it, among them
# `halyard-data/curl_trace.log` and `last_clients_main.json`. Those two hold a
# Bearer token and the streaming token: the AUTHENTICATION section below exists
# precisely to stop that, and an enumerated build-directory list had quietly
# cancelled it. Same lesson as the captures rule above, same fix.
build_*/
*/build_*/
**/build/
builddir
libromfs-generator
build_libromfs_generator
**/CMakeFiles/
**/CMakeCache.txt
**/*.o
**/*.a
**/cmake_install.cmake
**/Makefile
!CMakeLists.txt

# --- compiled outputs ---
*.elf
*.nso
*.nsp
*.nro
*.self
*.vpk
*.nacp
*.dksh
*.suprx

# --- vendored libraries (checked out, not committed; submodules are step 5) ---
third_party/borealis/
third_party/libopus/
third_party/wolfssl/
third_party/curl/
third_party/ffmpeg/
# No longer fetched (the WebRTC path and the QUIC trial, removed 2026-09-26),
# but older checkouts still hold them: keep them out of `git status`.
third_party/libdatachannel/
third_party/libjuice/
third_party/libsrtp/
third_party/ngtcp2/

# --- official clients downloaded for RE (they belong in the lab) ---
*.dmg
*.deb
*.exe
*.AppImage
*.msi
*.xapk
*.i64

# --- Ghidra databases (regenerable, huge) ---
**/*.rep/
**/*.gpr
**/*.lock
**/projectState.xml

# --- THE RUNTIME DATA DIRECTORY. ---
# `SHADOW_DATA_DIR` holds what the running application writes: the logs, the
# device identity, the saved REST responses - and `last_clients_main.json`
# carries the STREAMING TOKEN while `curl_trace.log` carries whole
# authenticated HTTP exchanges, Bearer headers included.
#
# It was covered only by accident, because it happens to sit inside a build
# directory. Named here so it is covered WHEREVER it lands: on a desktop
# checkout the data directory can be configured anywhere, and the one that was
# not inside a build directory was not ignored at all.
halyard-data/
**/halyard-data/

# --- AUTHENTICATION. Never committed, under any name. ---
*shadow_jwt*
*streaming_token*
*refresh_token*
# FT3 2026-10-02 - the SFTP credential, written only when SHADOW_FT_REVEAL=1.
# It is an SSH password granting READ AND WRITE on the VM's whole filesystem
# (the server confines no SFTP path). The application removes it when the
# session ends normally; a crash leaves it behind, which is exactly the case
# this line is for.
sftp.txt
# The saved REST responses and HTTP traces, by name as well as by directory.
# One pattern has already cancelled this whole policy once (see the captures
# rule at the top), so the files that carry a token are named twice on purpose.
last_clients_*.json
last_vm_ip_response.txt
curl_trace.log
proximus_trace.log
.shadow/
# The desktop client's session token: a backup copy, because /tmp gets cleaned.
.jeton/
# HAR files carry whole authenticated sessions, headers included.
*.har

# --- large debug output (regenerable by re-running) ---
**/strace.log
**/shadow_chunks.bin
**/shadow_frame_*.ppm
**/shadow_cuda.log
**/webrtc.log
**/webrtc_prev.log
*.err
*.log.old
# Intermediate output of the migration tool (comment-block extraction). Three
# were committed by mistake on 2026-09-02: 150 KB nobody reads, ageing beside
# the code they describe.
*.comments

# --- cache / IDE / OS / temp ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
/tmp/
*.bak
*.stock-bak
tools/switch-ftp.env

# Worktrees and scratch state of the assistant tooling.
.claude/
third_party/jansson/
.vita-ip

# Output of the PS Vita tools (tools/vita-push.sh) and libraries built
# out-of-band: these are not versioned, they are rebuilt.
config.txt.vita.bak
/vita-logs/
/vita-dumps/

# Build artefacts of the RE hook - rebuilt by its own scripts.
recon/tls_hook/*.so

# A hook plaintext log carries the ed25519 SFTP key, JWTs and Bearer tokens.
# docs/WSL2_WOLFSSL_HOOK_SETUP.md used to point its output here, inside the
# checkout, where nothing ignored it.
recon/captures/
# The English name of the credential directory tools/campaign_latency.sh
# documents. Only the French-era `.jeton/` was covered, so `.token/device.uuid`
# was one `git add -A` away from being published.
.token/

# vitacompanion is somebody else -- install it from upstream.
third_party/vitacompanion/

# A compiled test helper; build it from virtual_gamepad.c.
tools/test/virtual_gamepad

# the website, built by tools/build-site.py
/_site/
